Message-ID: <zEVjQogS1j8.en0Vl-nCU2cJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <zEVjQogS1j8.H1v6o_q4n3oJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
References: <zEVjQogS1j8.H1v6o_q4n3oJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/zEVjQogS1j8/m/en0Vl-nCU2cJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

You have both regression dependencies and covariances in the model.  Given the regression paths, the covariance statements tell lavaan that you want to covary predictors with the residuals from the same regressions .  Such a model will not be identified (without instrumental variables).  The lavaan error message says, "Surely that is a syntax error."
--Ed Rigdon

